Subject: virtual-io: hand a fused wait to a suspend hook

block_on is the choke point of every blocking WASIX syscall. It now wraps
the wait in a fused future pinned on the caller's stack and offers it to
a hook before parking. A runtime that runs guests on suspendable
coroutines installs the hook to suspend the caller instead of parking
its OS thread; the wait is then polled by whoever resumed the coroutine.
Fusing matters because a forked child re-creates each wait from its
future and may re-poll one that had already completed. Without a hook
nothing changes.

